BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Women's Wine Club
UID:event_314652352@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260509T035220Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T160000
SUMMARY:Summer Succulent Terrarium Class and Wine Tasting at 4th Street Ce
 llars
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma County Women's Wine Club (SCWWC)\nSummer is here in Win
 e Country and we are feeling Crafty!\n\nI have the pleasure of setting up 
 a fantastic orb Terrarium workshop offered through Flourish Petaluma and w
 ine tasting at 4th Street Cellars in Santa Rosa.\n\nIf you haven't been to
  Fourth Street Cellars\, you can experience the history of Railroad Square
  paired with the elegance of wine with its own history. Their wines are al
 l handcrafted by third generation grower and winemaker\, John Bambury whos
 e [Bonneau](https://www.bamburywinecollection.com/bonneau-wine/)\, [Egret]
 (https://www.bamburywinecollection.com/egret-wine/)\, and [Opal Moon](http
 s://www.bamburywinecollection.com/opal-moon-wine/) wines reflect their pro
 venance. They specialize in Pinot Noir\, Cabernet Sauvignon\, Zinfandel\, 
 and Chardonnay. You are welcome to purchase wine outside of the tasting pr
 ovided or become a wine member.\n\n**Get ready for a hands-on\, creative w
 orkshop where you'll dive into the art of designing and caring for succule
 nts.**\n\nWe will be arranging individual terrariums\, chatting\, and samp
 ling wine for 2-3 hours. You will have the option to choose from a wide va
 riety of succulents\, colorful pebbles\, and vibrant mosses to personalize
  your own Orb Terrarium. Brandi\, the owner of Flourish will provide exper
 t guidance\, care tips\, and plenty of hands-on support throughout the pro
 cess. Everyone will be able to take their terrariums home after the event.
 \n\nThere is a minimum of 10 people needed\, a maximum of 20 people\, plus
  this is a Co-ed event\, so both men and women are welcome. Your spot is r
 eserved by prepaying for your ticket through Daima Phipps\, co-hostess.\n\
 nThe cost of the event is $61\, which includes the slush fund\, plus whate
 ver wine you choose to purchase. They provide terrarium materials and guid
 ance on succulents\, plus care tips. We are asking that you reserve your s
 pot by prepaying just for the terrarium workshop\, which is $60. You can p
 ay for the wine tasting there\, by purchasing wine by the glass or as a se
 t tasting. We ask that members pay $1 per event into our "slush" fund to h
 elp us pay for incidentals for the group.\n\nGuests are welcome\, they wil
 l need to pre-pay as well. I suggest you wear layers as we might be outsid
 e\, and sometimes the weather is windy or cold. We will confirm headcount 
 about a week before.\n\nCheers to this fun succulent event!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/sonoma-county-womens-wine-club/events
 /314652352/
